    <ul>
      <li><strong>Ibn Hishām al-Anṣārī</strong>, <span class="ar" lang="ar" dir="rtl">قطر الندى وبل الصدى</span> (<em>Qaṭr al-Nadā wa-Ball al-Ṣadā</em>) and <span class="ar" lang="ar" dir="rtl">أوضح المسالك</span> (<em>Awḍaḥ al-Masālik</em>) — the chapters on the mubtadaʾ and khabar, the licensors of an indefinite subject, and obligatory fronting.</li>
      <li><strong>Ibn ʿAqīl</strong>, <span class="ar" lang="ar" dir="rtl">شرح ابن عقيل على ألفية ابن مالك</span> (his commentary on Ibn Mālik's <em>Alfiyya</em>) — on governance by al-ibtidāʾ and on the omitted predicate behind a quasi-sentence.</li>
      <li><strong>Al-Ashmūnī</strong>, <span class="ar" lang="ar" dir="rtl">شرح الأشموني على الألفية</span> — for the finer disagreements over what exactly raises the khabar.</li>
